              "name": "lutzflcat"
            },
            "reviewBody": "5.2.20 I dissolved the sugar in the bourdon and lemon juice and then poured over the ice. A nice Saturday evening cocktail, and it does taste somewhat similar to a whisky sour."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "BrightGin9139"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I love bourbon during the winter, and this is a refreshing cocktail. Instead of sugar, I used a homemade citrus sweetener my daughter-in-law made. It takes too long for the sugar to dissolve. The other option is to dissolve the sugar in a small amount of warm water or warm the lemon juice first, then add the sugar to dissolve. Either way this is a great cocktail.",
